 ### SCENARIO-PHASE4-082: Exp4350 Either Reproduces ka59 L1 Or Records An Honest Continuation Partial
 **Description:** Running Exp 4350 either writes `blocked_offline_env_missing_ka59` when the local ka59 simulator is absent, writes `success_e3_ka59_L1_reproduced` only when the refined induced-model plan is execution-grounded and independently reproduces at least L1 offline, or writes `complete_e3_ka59_partial_model_<acc>` when the bounded explore-verify-plan attempt does not reach the reproduced-L1 gate. A successful run MUST set `offline_reproduced=true`, `reproduced_levels>=1`, `plan_executed=true`, `explore_lemmas_collected>0`, `verifier_is_oracle=true`, preserve the world model path and hash, and compute the reproducibility checksum from the world model hash, plan, reproduction result, verifier rounds, and explore lemma count. A partial run MUST set `offline_reproduced=false`, `reproduced_levels=0`, preserve `verifier_accuracy_per_round` and `explore_lemmas_collected`, preserve the world model path and hash, report the best verifier accuracy and residual mismatch class, and record the residual mismatch as a missing-world-model-rule gap rather than claiming a solve.
+
+### REQ-PHASE4-083: ARC-AGI-3 E3 Deeper Solved-Games Multi-Target Exp4351
+**Description:** The system SHALL run Exp 4351 as an offline, no-leaderboard multi-target deepen pass over `sc25`, `tn36`, and `ar25`, checkpointing the targets in that order so a bounded window preserves prior target results. It MUST first confirm that `environment_files/sc25/`, `environment_files/tn36/`, and `environment_files/ar25/` are non-empty, that the ARC executable-world-model and reproduction-gate harnesses import, that TRM training is stood down, and that `scripts/research_conductor.py` is not modified; if any target simulator is missing, the workflow MUST record `blocked_offline_env_missing_<game>` for that target and continue the others without leaderboard submission. For each available target it MUST print and persist per-target per-round verifier accuracy, preserve the world-model or solver deliverable path, and accept a level only when it is beyond that target's prior reproduced best and `arc_solver_kit.reproduce()` reports `reproduced=true`. The `tn36` target MUST reuse the timed spike-trap program-editor solver path through L7; `sc25` and `ar25` MUST report honest partials if their bounded deepen attempts do not reproduce a new level beyond L1. The terminal artifact `results/experiment_4351_e3_deeper_solved_games.json` MUST include `honest_verdict`, `per_target_scorecard`, `reproducible_total_levels`, `new_levels_reproduced`, `world_model_paths`, `verifier_is_oracle`, `preconditions_checked`, `random_seed`, and `reproducibility_checksum`, with `reproducible_total_levels`, `new_levels_reproduced`, and `verifier_is_oracle` emitted as bare values rather than principle-wrapped dictionaries. The artifact field principles SHALL be exactly: `honest_verdict` = `Terminal-prefixed (success_e3_deeper_<targets>_reproduced or complete_e3_deeper_partial). Any NEW reproduced level on any target is progress; an honest partial across all three is also progress.`; `per_target_scorecard` = `list of {game, prior_best_level, new_reproduced_level, verifier_accuracy, offline_reproduced} -- the per-target breadth-of-progress record (sc25/ar25/tn36).`; `reproducible_total_levels` = `BARE int: the ARC reproducible-level count after this task (>= the prior 21) -- the monotonic north-star accuracy signal; sc25 L2+ is the biggest single upside (+4 possible).`; `new_levels_reproduced` = `BARE int: NEW levels offline-reproduced this task across the three targets -- the incremental-progress unit.`; `world_model_paths` = `list[str]: the extended world-model / solver paths (the deliverables).`; `verifier_is_oracle` = `BARE bool=true -- the SOLVEs are execution-grounded; ARC progress, NOT a moat headline.`; `preconditions_checked` = `Records the offline-env presence per target + harness import + TRM-stand-down; pre-empts the silent-missing-resource fabrication mode.`; `random_seed` = `Determinism precondition for the induction + exploration + planning.`; and `reproducibility_checksum` = `Hash of the extended models + the plans + the reproduce() results; lets a third party re-run.`
+
+### SCENARIO-PHASE4-083: Exp4351 Banks New Reproduced Deeper Levels Or Records Honest Per-Target Partials
+**Description:** Running Exp 4351 either writes `success_e3_deeper_<targets>_reproduced` when at least one target independently reproduces a new level beyond its prior best via `arc_solver_kit.reproduce()`, or writes `complete_e3_deeper_partial` when all available targets complete their bounded checkpoint attempts without a new reproduced level. A successful run MUST set `new_levels_reproduced>=1`, `reproducible_total_levels>=21`, `verifier_is_oracle=true`, include exactly one `per_target_scorecard` row for each of `sc25`, `tn36`, and `ar25`, preserve `world_model_paths`, set `submitted_to_leaderboard=false`, and compute the reproducibility checksum from the target rows, deliverable hashes, plans, reproduction-gate results, and random seed. A partial run MUST preserve the same scorecard shape, set `offline_reproduced=false` for targets that did not advance beyond their prior best, record each target's best verifier accuracy and residual win-mechanic gap class, and record any missing environment as `blocked_offline_env_missing_<game>` without blocking the remaining targets.
